From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:07:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pinctrl: samsung: allow GPIO hogs in a GPIO bank

A board may need to hold a line at a fixed level from boot, as the
Pixel 6 Pro holds TS_SPI_SEL low so that the touch controller's SPI bus
belongs to the AP rather than the AoC. Allow gpio-hog child nodes in a
bank, as gpio.yaml describes them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/pinctrl/samsung,pinctrl-gpio-bank.yaml         | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/samsung,pinctrl-gpio-bank.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/samsung,pinctrl-gpio-bank.yaml
index 8cf3c47ab..20bfb3d2b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/samsung,pinctrl-gpio-bank.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/samsung,pinctrl-gpio-bank.yaml
@@ -45,6 +45,12 @@ properties:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 8
 
+patternProperties:
+  '-hog(-[0-9]+)?$':
+    type: object
+    required:
+      - gpio-hog
+
 required:
   - '#gpio-cells'
   - gpio-controller
